WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.005
In Omni Dispatch, open Chat.

00:00:02.185 --> 00:00:05.535
Direct Messages lists your individual conversations.

00:00:05.715 --> 00:00:08.531
Channels and incident rooms are listed separately.

00:00:08.711 --> 00:00:11.463
For this exercise, select Matthew Casey.

00:00:11.783 --> 00:00:13.959
Check the name at the top before you write.

00:00:14.139 --> 00:00:18.277
This is a direct conversation with Casey, who has
Omni I C open.

00:00:18.597 --> 00:00:23.163
Use the message field to say what is ready and what
you need the recipient to do.

00:00:23.343 --> 00:00:27.460
Here, Dispatch says Command can review the archived
station inspection.

00:00:27.640 --> 00:00:31.011
Leave Urgent off for this routine update and select
Send.

00:00:31.331 --> 00:00:34.360
The message now appears in the Dispatch conversation.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:36.631
That shows it was sent from this console.

00:00:36.811 --> 00:00:39.072
Check the recipient’s screen for delivery.

00:00:39.392 --> 00:00:44.320
On the I C console, Casey opens the direct
conversation with Wallace Boden.

00:00:44.500 --> 00:00:47.295
Here is the conversation before the new update.

00:00:47.615 --> 00:00:51.967
The inspection update appears in I C while the
conversation stays open.

00:00:52.147 --> 00:00:54.515
This confirms live delivery in the app.

00:00:54.695 --> 00:00:59.409
A device push alert is a separate check and depends
on the department’s push setup.

00:00:59.729 --> 00:01:04.103
Casey replies that the update arrived and that they
will review the inspection.

00:01:04.283 --> 00:01:09.424
In a real handoff, state what you received and what
you are taking responsibility for.

00:01:09.744 --> 00:01:14.843
Back in Dispatch, open the conversation to confirm
that the acknowledgment is saved.

00:01:15.023 --> 00:01:17.988
This gives both operators a record of the handoff.

00:01:18.168 --> 00:01:23.139
The same pattern works for a search base, a security
desk, or a field support team.
